<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Lineo's mark: three lines of a notepad column, and the rule they add up to.

    The name comes from *linea*, and `AGENTS.md` §1 asks that the idea stay visible in
    naming. It is visible here too — the icon is the product's one sentence, a document
    made of lines that resolve into an answer. The total is the widest and the heaviest
    stroke, set below a gap twice the others, so the eye reads a sum rather than a fourth
    entry.

    **Geometry.** The 108dp viewport is not the drawing area: a launcher masks the outer
    band and parallaxes what is left, so only the central 66dp circle — radius 33 about
    (54,54) — is guaranteed visible. Every stroke here, round caps included, stays inside
    a radius of 33. The caps extend `strokeWidth / 2` past each endpoint, which is why the
    lines start at x=34 rather than at the 31 they appear to.

    The same drawable is the `monochrome` layer for themed icons. The system replaces the
    colour and keeps the shape, and a mark that is four strokes has nothing to lose to
    that.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- The lines of the document, varying in length the way written ones do. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M34,36 L68,36"
        android:strokeColor="#646116"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeWidth="6" />
    <path
        android:pathData="M34,47 L58,47"
        android:strokeColor="#646116"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeWidth="6" />
    <path
        android:pathData="M34,58 L72,58"
        android:strokeColor="#646116"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeWidth="6" />

    <!-- The total: wider than any line above it, and heavier, after a deliberate gap. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M34,72 L74,72"
        android:strokeColor="#646116"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeWidth="8" />
</vector>
